config MIDDLEWARE_SIP
    bool "LAN SIP video call middleware"
    depends on LWIP
    default n
    help
      Self-implemented minimal SIP stack plus G.711 audio and MJPEG/RTP
      video, used for LAN peer-to-peer video calls between the device
      and a host program built from the same core sources
      (src/middleware/sip/host builds sip_peer on Ubuntu).

      - core/ is pure C (BSD sockets via sip_osal only) and is shared
        verbatim between the firmware and the host peer.
      - device/sip_service.c owns FreeRTOS tasks, the audio tap, the
        camera/JPEG pipeline and the call focus channel.

      Enable together with WIFI and LWIP in the application config.
